<h1>Lesson 5: Preparing for the Final Project</h1>
<div style="display: inline-block; background-color: #E4E2F8; color: #1F1976; font-weight: bold; padding: 4px 12px; border-radius: 10px; margin-bottom: 12px;">Aligns to curriculum Lesson 13</div>
<p>This module offers a brief overview of the key concepts and teaching strategies in each lesson, it isn't a replacement for reviewing each lesson in full before you teach it. Take your time with the individual lesson plans for a deeper dive.</p>
<p>This lesson prepares you to teach one curriculum lesson:</p>
<div style="background-color: #F7F7FB; border-left: 4px solid #4C42CF; border-radius: 8px; padding: 12px 16px; margin-bottom: 16px;">
<p><b>Curriculum Lesson 13:</b> Pixels of Me Project</p>
<a href="[LESSON 13 URL]" style="display: inline-block; background-color: #4C42CF; color: #FFFFFF; font-weight: bold; padding: 6px 14px; border-radius: 8px; text-decoration: none; margin-top: 6px; font-size: 13px;">View Curriculum Lesson 13</a>
</div>
<hr>
<p><b>By the end of this lesson, you'll:</b></p>
<p style="margin: 0 0 6px 0;">• Explore effective collaboration methods for guiding students through a final project</p>
<p style="margin: 0 0 6px 0;">• Preview structured feedback approaches you can use during peer review and gallery walks</p>
<p style="margin: 0;">• Look at planning techniques that help students manage their time and workflow</p>
<p style="margin: 16px 0 0 0;"><i>Suggested time: 10 minutes</i></p>
<hr>
